committer Mizuki Hayashi <mizuki@kamiyo.ai> 1792161943 +0200

fix(v16): start the side resets when an asset is left with no legs

Unilateral reduces subtract the opposite side's OI exactly but floor its
A index, so a side's OI can sit one or more units above its legs'
effective quantities, and Recovery forfeits never start the zero-OI side
reset. Once a side has no stored leg, its leftover OI carries no loss
weight (spec.md:953) and the leg clear cannot remove it, since it
refuses more than a leg's raw basis; the side never resets, and
retire_empty_asset and restart refuse the empty asset, also after
resolution when no leg is left to detach. begin_zero_oi_residue_resets
now first drops that OI: before resolution only when the whole asset is
legless and neither side has a pending loss barrier, so both sides reach
zero together and Live OI stays equal, and after resolution from each
legless side without a barrier. The trade close-out, rebalance,
liquidation and resolved detach paths already call it; Recovery forfeit
clears and the auto-crank release of a pending obligation now call it
too, and so do the close ledger advance and the cure once they clear a
barrier on a legless asset. An asset that an older engine already left
legless with leftover OI is out of scope. Neither the resolved payout
path nor bankruptcy booking reads OI, so payouts do not change. The
zero-OI reset harness now models the drop.

Fixes #238.
